  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Africa Food Crisis</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Given the unprecedented level of food insecurity across the African continent (with over 65 million people currently experiencing acute food insecurity= IPC phase 3-5), the ESA team and WCA team have decided to adopt a holistic approach to the Hunger Crisis. This programme page will serve as a location to save documents and decisions relevant to the overall crisis, whereas information pertinent to specific geographic locations will be saved on the Emergency pages already created for those situations.
Projections show food insecurity numbers rapidly increasing with some countries facing a risk of famine (IPC phase 5) in 2022: Nigeria, Ethiopia, South Sudan&#x200B;. Ever increasing levels of malnutrition: already over 11 million children acutely malnourished in the Sahel and Horn of Africa with about 30% cases of severe acute malnutrition&#x200B;. The IFRC has launched emergency appeals for Kenya, Ethiopia, Somalia and Nigeria.</narrative>
  </description>
